// generated by tools/make-patch.js from README.txt - do not edit
const PATCHNOTES=[["0.9.115","Skyfall Warden: it now takes off again 5 seconds after landing on its perch. A shared timer in the enemy code kept resetting its perch timer, so it stayed down forever.","2026-10-26T17:29:02.279Z"],["0.9.114","Patch notes: fixed the list stopping early and entries being merged together. They are now ordered by release date and time (newest first) instead of by version number.","2026-10-26T17:18:28.181Z"],["0.9.113","Native renderer fix: its shader list was out of date, so the game's shaders were rejected and the native renderer never showed a picture. The list is rebuilt for the current game. It also no longer turns itself off just because you quit from the menu early: it counts as working after 8 seconds, gets one more try after a bad start, and an earlier automatic turn-off is retried once.","2026-10-26T17:18:00.516Z"],["0.9.112","Settings > General: new Show Debug UI option. A strip along the top of the screen shows the frame rate, whether the native renderer is working, DLSS and ray tracing status, and when and why anything failed.",""],["0.9.111","The renderer fallback now needs 60 frames in a row to fail (was 30), and Settings keeps showing the Graphics API you picked even if the native renderer could not start (the reason is shown under it).",""],["0.9.110","Native renderer: the game now ignores the old ANGLE \"Vulkan\" graphics API while the native renderer is on (it could stop the native renderer from starting), and Settings shows why the native renderer turned itself off.",""],["0.9.109","Skyfall Warden: its perch now really lands. It flies to a spot beside you, sets its talons on the floor and sits completely still for 3.5 seconds (it was hovering a few feet up and drifting), so melee builds can hit it.",""],["0.9.108","Settings: the Rendering and Native renderer sections are merged. Pick \"API: Vulkan (native renderer)\" in the Graphics API list and the DLSS and ray traced shadow options appear right there.",""],["0.9.107","Monster blood is now green (hit splatters, the death explosion, wall and floor splats, and the pool), and a dying monster leaves one pool, right where it died, instead of several (one had ended up on top of a wall). Human blood stays red.",""],["0.9.106","Monsters now burst in a gory mess when killed: flying chunks, a spray of blood in every direction that splatters walls and floor, and several pools (bigger for big monsters and bosses). Humans, the robot, knights, aliens and power armor are unchanged.",""],["0.9.105","Fixed Energy Shield draining every shield you had, from any source (shop shield, Shield Dispenser, Super Shield...). Now only the Energy Shield's own 50 (+25 per copy) drains, 1 per second; shield from other sources stays.",""],["0.9.104","The ability key boxes at the bottom right now use short labels (LS, RS, LC, RC, LA, RA, Spc, Ins, Del...) so long key names no longer overflow and overlap the icon.",""],["0.9.103","You can now put several actions on the same key. Settings > Controls warns you (a message when you set it, an amber key button, and a Shared keys line at the top), and pressing the key does all of them. Before, binding a key that was already in use swapped the two actions, and power overrides refused keys that were taken.",""],["0.9.102","Your magazine (and your second weapon's) is refilled when you move on to the next floor. The Loot Box messages now say to open them from Customize Profile > Cosmetics.",""],["0.9.101","Taking Extended Mags now fills your magazine to the new maximum straight away (and your second weapon's, if you carry one), so you do not have to reload first.",""],["0.9.100","The Loot Boxes button in Customize Profile is now called Cosmetics (and the screen is titled Cosmetics). When you have unopened Loot Boxes the button turns gold and says how many.",""],["0.9.99","Customize Profile redesigned: Loot Boxes button now at the top next to your name, and Skin, Spray and Background are tidy cards with short descriptions, a preview, a status line and Upload / Remove buttons (Template for skins).",""],["0.9.98","New Encyclopedia on the main menu (where Loot Boxes was): a page for every weapon, power and boss/enemy type, with a rotating picture, value ranges, falloff, how powers stack and their maximums, plus Terms (Blazing, Frostbitten, Explosive, weapon words, minor mods, status effects) and Basics. Numbers are read from the game's own tables. Loot Boxes moved into Customize Profile (the main menu's Customize Profile button turns gold with a count while you have unopened boxes).",""],["0.9.97","Weapon pick screens (solo, co-op, deathmatch) now show a short plain-words line under each weapon's name, e.g. \"Close-range shotgun blast\", so new players get what each gun is like before reading the numbers.",""],["0.9.96","A single error while drawing a frame no longer switches the game permanently to the plain software renderer (which is what makes flat blood splatters stand up half-buried and drops all shadows). The game now skips that frame and only gives up after 30 errors in a row; the last error is kept in window.GLR_LASTERR. If ground splatters or character shadows still look wrong, send native\\bin\\arb-rt-log.txt.",""],["0.9.95","With hardware ray tracing on, shadows from moving things are now done by the ray tracing itself: each frame the characters' real 3D models, props, chests and turrets (and a solid body for monsters drawn as flat images) are added to the ray tracing scene, so they cast and receive shadows on everything. Needs the native renderer rebuilt (PUBLISH.bat does it) and the updated shader pack. Without ray tracing the 0.9.94 shadows are used.",""],["0.9.94","Characters now cast real traced shadows: the player, monsters, humans and allies are tested by the shadow rays (hardware ray tracing and the normal path alike), so their shadows fall on the floor, walls and props. The simple ground shadows from 0.9.93 are now only used when light shadows are off. Updates the native shader pack.",""],["0.9.93","The player, monsters, humans, allies and turrets now cast shadows on the floor on every normal floor (stretched away from the sun or the nearest lamp, plus a small dark patch under the feet), so they no longer look pasted on, with or without ray tracing. Shadows are a bit subtle on very dark floors.",""],["0.9.92","Fixed the Coliseum (and any floor after a lit one) being mostly dark with odd window-shaped light patches when ray tracing is off: the shadow grid from the previous floor was being reused instead of the new floor's.",""],["0.9.91","The Second Weapon power now has a 3D shop model (two pistols pointing opposite ways) when it is on a shelf.",""],["0.9.90","The three weapons offered by the Second Weapon power are now three different weapon types, and never the type you are already holding.",""],["0.9.89","The Second Weapon power now lists your two weapons at the bottom right, the same place and style as Bomb Defusal (it sits just above your ability boxes when you have abilities).",""],["0.9.88","New rare power, Second Weapon (singleplayer and co-op): carry two weapons. When you take it you pick one of three rolled weapons, like at the start of a run. Swap between them with the scroll wheel or the 1 and 2 keys; both weapons are listed on the HUD.",""],["0.9.87","Co-op: players in the same shop, library or arcade now see each other and share the same shelves (the same stock for everyone, and an item someone buys is gone for the others). Dismemberment now works in co-op and every player sees the same limbs come off. Limbs now match the kill: a leg shot takes a leg, a body shot an arm, a head shot the head (blade kills still take limbs at random). Hosts need this version.",""],["0.9.86","Co-op fixes: the shop, library and arcade can now be entered in co-op (each player shops on their own, is hidden from the others while inside, and earns money from monster kills); the moving yellow squares on the co-op minimap are gone (teammates already show as green arrows); boss floors in co-op now offer the rare power choices; deaths to monsters in co-op no longer say 'killed by the void'. Hosts need this version for the shop-hiding to reach other players.",""],["0.9.85","All power cooldowns reset to ready when you go through the next floor portal. Ember Rounds can now be taken up to 5 times while you hold the Flamethrower, each stack adding another burn of damage.",""],["0.9.84","Burn effects now stack: a Blazing weapon and Ember Rounds each burn on their own, so an enemy can have up to 2 burns at once for double burn damage.",""],["0.9.83","Fixed the lag when deflecting a lot of projectiles at once (deflect sounds and sparks are now capped per frame and the target search runs once per frame). Acid robots no longer bleed: they throw sparks instead of blood and leave no blood pool.",""],["0.9.82","Dismemberment: a killing blow can now take limbs off humanoid enemies and players. Blades slice arms, legs and heads off, big overkill (shotguns, blasts) tears them away, and a shot can take off the part it hit. Each severed limb tumbles and bounces as its own piece, the stump bleeds, and the pieces stay on the floor. Turned off with the ragdoll setting.",""],["0.9.81","The end of run screen now has three options: Roll again, Main menu and Close game.",""],["0.9.80","Fixed Vhaloru's (floor 15 boss) regular projectiles: they now launch from chest height, aim at you, and show as large glowing plasma orbs instead of tiny dim dots near the floor.",""],["0.9.79","New blood: hits and kills spray droplets that fly, land and stain the ground (flat splatters turned the way they were thrown) and walls (with drips); bodies leave a pool. Replaces the single round sprite.",""],["0.9.78","City floors are now lit by street lamps along the kerb (spaced out, never in front of doors or at junctions) instead of wall lamps on the buildings.",""],["0.9.77","Opened chests no longer leave an invisible solid block behind on True 3D levels. The shop is now lit by its ceiling light panels (brighter, more even).",""],["0.9.76","Fixed the Crimson/Ashen Knight's shockwave projectiles vanishing the instant they appeared on True 3D levels (floors 5 and 10).",""],["0.9.75","Coliseum: monsters (including the summoner's minions) now only appear on open arena sand, never in the stands or walls. The sun now lights the coliseum and casts shadows (Lighting setting). Cursed chests no longer push a power past its max.",""],["0.9.74","Tab menu with many powers: wider 4-column list that uses the whole screen, taller, with a clearly visible scrollbar (also on the multiplayer scoreboard).",""],["0.9.73","Escape in Settings goes back (to the pause menu or title); Escape again closes the pause menu.",""],["0.9.72","Settings groups now fold open and closed (all closed by default, remembers what you opened). Death screen map now fills its square on small maps.",""],["0.9.71","Settings redesigned: grouped cards, one row per setting (name left, control right), short hints instead of paragraphs, cleaner sliders and checkboxes. All options unchanged.",""],["0.9.70","Dynamic lighting now also affects the player's gun and hands (ambient darkening plus nearby lights, muzzle flash included), and monster sprites now get the same ambient level and light strength as the 3D surfaces. Humans and props were already lit.",""],["0.9.69","Hardware ray tracing (optional, native renderer): Settings > Native renderer > Ray tracing. The graphics card's ray tracing hardware now does the dynamic-light shadows (soft edges) instead of the software voxel version, using the level's real triangles. Needs a ray tracing card (RTX etc.) and the lighting setting Lights + ray-traced shadows. Also: the scratch-off Decline button is smaller.",""],["0.9.68","Fixed the coliseum gate (floors 5 and 10) staying shut during the boss cutscene and then jumping open when it ended; it now rises during the cutscene.",""],["0.9.67","Scratch-off tickets: when a ticket wins, a Decline prize button appears at the bottom right of the ticket. The prize is only handed over when you close the ticket, so you can turn it down.",""],["0.9.66","Fixed the coliseum gate (floors 5 and 10) showing as a block of yellow hazard stripes instead of stone.",""],["0.9.65","Native renderer: the log (native\\bin\\arb-rt-log.txt) now records where its window is and what covers it, to track down a case where the 3D picture did not show behind the game's menus and HUD.",""],["0.9.64","Native renderer now draws straight to the screen in its own window behind the game (borderless fullscreen while on), which removes the stutter from copying every frame through the browser. Adds optional NVIDIA DLSS (Settings > Native renderer > DLSS On/Off + quality; needs an RTX card). Hardware ray tracing is not in yet. Untested on real hardware at release: send native\\bin\\arb-rt-log.txt if anything looks wrong. The update from GitHub now includes the native renderer (arb-rt.exe, nvngx_dlss.dll, shader pack), so players need no extra steps.",""],["0.9.63","Optional native Vulkan renderer (experimental, Windows). Settings > Rendering > Native renderer draws the game with a separate Vulkan program (native/arb-rt) instead of the browser; run native\\BUILD-NATIVE.bat once to build it. It replays the game's real frames pixel-for-pixel in tests and falls back to the normal renderer on any problem. It already carries the motion vectors and jitter DLSS needs, but DLSS and hardware ray tracing are NOT switched on in the game yet (the probe showed both work on an RTX 4070 SUPER).",""],["0.9.62","Software rendering is gone: the game always uses your graphics card (if the GPU process crashes on Windows it retries once with a different graphics API). New: real light sources. Lamps now sit on walls and light the area around them, and explosions flash. Settings > Lighting adds optional ray-traced shadows (done in the shader, works on any card, off by default). Also added the start of the optional native renderer in the native folder, for real NVIDIA DLSS and hardware ray tracing on cards that support them. It is only a test tool for now (BUILD-NATIVE.bat, RUN-PROBE.bat) and is not used by the game yet.",""],["0.9.61","Fixed sprays (K) doing nothing on the singleplayer maps that run in the true 3D engine. The check that stops you spraying on the floor was reading the floor inside the wall and always refusing; it now reads it just in front of the wall.",""],["0.9.60","Ragdoll bodies can no longer pass through themselves. Legs, arms, torso and head now push each other apart, so a leg cannot go through the torso, legs cannot cross through each other, and limbs have to rest on or against the body instead.",""],["0.9.59","Real 3D people, fuller ragdolls, melee enemies. (1) Human models (you, other players and human enemies) are now real 3D models with the skin wrapped on them, hats and capes included, when they are close; far away they stay flat pictures. Team outlines still work. Settings > Rendering > Real 3D characters turns this off. (2) Ragdolls use the whole skin and all cosmetics, and follow the ground so they no longer sink through city sidewalks and kerbs. (3) About one in four singleplayer human enemies now fight with a melee weapon (axe, hammer, sword or daggers): they run at you and swing. Knights, aliens, robots and foxes are unchanged.",""],["0.9.58","Ragdoll and chest fixes. (1) Ragdolls no longer slide through walls in the true 3D levels (city buildings and every other level); they now stop against walls and slide along them. (2) Ragdolls now look like the person they came from: characters with a custom skin keep their face, hair, sleeves, hands and trousers colours from that skin, and everyone gets the right hair style and colour and the team-colour marker. Hats and capes are still not shown on ragdolls. (3) Battle Royale chests no longer leave an invisible solid block behind once they are opened or taken; you and the bots can walk through the spot.",""],["0.9.57","Fixed shots missing or doing no damage against people. After the first hit on a human enemy or another player, the hit reaction (the flinch) overwrote that character's hit radius, so every later shot at them passed straight through until they were killed or reloaded. Hit reactions still play, and shots now land every time you hit.",""],["0.9.56","True 3D levels, final stage. Battle Royale is now a true 3D world too (hills, buildings with doors, windows, decks, stairs and roofs, trees, rocks, sun shadows), so every level and mode in the game now runs on the one 3D engine. Settings > Graphics > True 3D levels still switches back to the old grid and terrain engines if something looks wrong.",""],["0.9.55","True 3D levels, second stage. Deathmatch, team modes, CTF, co-op, Bomb Defusal and every other online mode now run on the true 3D levels, bots included. The Foundry crushers are real moving 3D slabs, the Coliseum (arena, seating, rising gate, boss intro) is 3D, and the shops, library and arcade are 3D. Only Battle Royale still uses the old terrain engine. Settings > Graphics > True 3D levels turns the whole thing off.",""],["0.9.54","True 3D levels, first stage. The normal singleplayer floors (Dungeon, Cavern, Lab, Crypt, Manor, Mineshaft, City, Hideout) are now built as real 3D worlds, the same engine the imported maps use, but look and play the same as before: same layout, textures, fog, props, pits, acid, jumping, enemies and shots. Still on the old flat grid for now: online and deathmatch games, the Foundry, Coliseum, Battle Royale and shop levels. Settings > Graphics > True 3D levels turns it off if something is wrong.",""],["0.9.53","Killcams: bullets no longer hang in the air; they keep flying and vanish like they do in the game. Skyfall Warden (floor 25): every 12 seconds he lands next to you and perches for 3 seconds, unarmed and mending 10 HP per second, so melee weapons can reach him, then takes off again.",""],["0.9.52","Hit reactions: when you shoot a human (enemy or another player) the part you hit reacts. An arm whips away, a leg buckles and the body dips, the head snaps back, and a chest hit makes the whole upper body fold, then it springs back. Ragdoll bodies now rest on raised ground such as the city sidewalks instead of sinking into it, and are thrown a little harder than in 0.9.51 (about 20% more).",""],["0.9.51","The fan gun and the pistol now kick when they fire (their recoil was never triggered in 0.9.49), and ragdoll bodies are thrown a bit less far.",""],["0.9.50","Fixed a bug from 0.9.49 that made the gun turn into a flat 2D drawing whenever you reloaded. Reloads are 3D again.",""],["0.9.49","Ragdoll bodies: when a human dies (singleplayer, co-op and multiplayer) their body is now thrown by the hit, tumbles and settles on the floor instead of vanishing. There is a new Ragdolls option in Settings to turn it off. Gun feel: every shot now kicks the gun back and recovers with a smooth spring, the gun lags a little behind your mouse movement, the pistol slide cycles and locks back when empty, the marksman rifle cycles its operating rod and pings when its clip runs out, and the sniper rifle works its bolt after each shot. Pistols, the marksman rifle, the rattler and twin fangs eject brass. Reloads now play matching sounds (magazine out and in, slide release, shells, bolt, energy cells, fuel tank).",""],["0.9.48","Gun reload animations rebuilt. Every gun now has its own smooth, keyframed reload instead of one shared tilt: the pistol drops its magazine and slaps in a new one with a slide release, the coach gun breaks open, ejects its shells and thumbs in new ones before snapping shut, and the Needler, Rattler, Lance, Hand cannon, Marksman, Sniper, Flamethrower and Fan gun each get a support hand that brings in the right part (crystal cartridge, drum, energy cell, speedloader, clip, magazine, fuel canister) at its own angle. All moves ease in and out. Twin fangs and melee weapons keep their previous animations.",""],["0.9.47","Co-op: the host now tells everyone which monsters are still alive every 1.5 seconds, and any copy that is not on the list (because its death message was missed) is removed. This fixes dead monsters showing up for another player that you cannot hurt.",""],["0.9.46","Co-op: monsters now use the same floor-by-floor health scaling as singleplayer, with 33% more health for every additional player (replaces the flat +33% from 0.9.44).",""],["0.9.45","Co-op: the death screen no longer says \"You fell into a pit\" for deaths that had nothing to do with a pit (the message from an earlier fall was never cleared), and damage that was still queued from the previous floor is dropped when a new floor starts.",""],["0.9.44","Co-op: monsters and bosses have 33% more health.",""],["0.9.43","Co-op: players who are not the host took far more damage than the host from the same attacks (every pellet of a shotgun blast, every tick of fire, landed in full because they had no invulnerability after a hit). They now get the same 0.2 s of protection after each hit as the host, which should stop the sudden deaths.",""],["0.9.42","Multiplayer lobby: the Wingman layout option now appears only after the host has imported a CS:GO map that has one (ticking it re-imports the map), instead of being there all the time.",""],["0.9.41","Halloween mode: the shop gets cobwebs, a purple tint and spooky decorations, the shopkeeper becomes a witch, and a pumpkin sits on the main menu.",""],["0.9.40","Halloween mode: from October 24 to October 31 (singleplayer only) props look spookier with a purple tint and cobwebs, pumpkins, ghosts, tombstones, bats, candles, skulls and spiders are scattered around every map, human enemies wear a skeleton skin, and quiet silly spooky music plays on maps that have no music of their own. Set ld_hal to 0 in local storage to turn it off.",""],["0.9.39","Custom CS:S maps (e.g. wingman maps): when a map lists more bomb sites than are reachable from the spawns, the unreachable ones are dropped, so Defuse mode only uses the real site.",""],["0.9.38","Counter-Strike: Source maps (de_dust2): the window patches are set slightly behind the wall face, so they no longer flicker or draw lines where they overlap the wall.",""],["0.9.37","Counter-Strike: Source maps (de_dust2): windows are now found from the wall faces themselves (a hole fully ringed by wall), and every window that lets you look into ground nobody can reach is shut with a patch of wall. Doorways you can walk through, and windows onto reachable ground, are left alone.",""],["0.9.36","Counter-Strike: Source maps (de_dust2): removed the window walls added in 0.9.34 and 0.9.35 (they put walls in open areas). The gate and door walls from 0.9.33 stay.",""],["0.9.35","Counter-Strike: Source maps (de_dust2): every window you can see through into somewhere nobody can walk (inaccessible rooms, sky) is now shut with a plain wall, so they can't be used to look through the map. Windows that look into ground you can reach stay open.",""],["0.9.34","Counter-Strike: Source maps (de_dust2): windows you could see empty sky through from the ground are now shut with a plain wall (drawn only). Windows that look into a room or onto the street stay open.",""],["0.9.33","Counter-Strike: Source maps (de_dust2): the big gates and doors (the temple entrance and the wooden doors) are now closed with a plain wall sized to the gap they sit in, instead of the earlier guess-based walls. Drawn only; walking is unchanged.",""],["0.9.32","The small (Wingman) layout option now only appears after a Counter-Strike: Global Offensive map that has one has been imported.",""],["0.9.31","Counter-Strike: Source maps: the new gate-cover walls were showing up as tall slabs in open areas. They are now only added where there really is a wide gap you can see empty void through, and short pieces that end in open air are dropped.",""],["0.9.30","Counter-Strike: Source maps (like de_dust2): big gates and doorways you could see right out of the map through are now covered with plain walls (drawn only, you still walk exactly where you did before). Nothing else about how these maps load changed.",""],["0.9.29","Fix: the Counter-Strike changes (map cropping, movement mask, simpler terrain, hidden-room culling, prop changes, no textures, lower resolution) now apply only to Counter-Strike: Global Offensive maps. Counter-Strike: Source, TF2 and other Source maps import exactly as they did before 0.9.10.",""],["0.9.28","Counter-Strike maps no longer load the Counter-Strike textures (the game draws its own stand-in textures); prop models are still read from the game files.",""],["0.9.27","Counter-Strike maps: prop models are cut to about half their triangles on import (shortest edges merged; open edges kept and no triangle turned inside out).",""],["0.9.26","Imported maps: flat terrain patches are built from far fewer triangles (any patch that stays within a unit and a half of the original keeps only the rows and columns it needs; collision is unchanged). Inferno went from 95,000 to 43,000 triangles.",""],["0.9.25","Counter-Strike maps are now drawn at no more than 960x540 worth of pixels.",""],["0.9.24","Counter-Strike maps are drawn at no more than 960x540 worth of pixels (stretched to the window) for speed; your own resolution comes back when you leave the map.",""],["0.9.23","Counter-Strike maps, framerate: Counter-Strike textures are drawn at a quarter of the pixels (64x64), and walls, floors and terrain in parts of the map you cannot see into are skipped using the map visibility data (checked pixel for pixel against drawing everything).",""],["0.9.22","Imported maps, framerate: props are drawn nearest first and a prop whose whole outline is hidden behind walls that are already drawn is skipped, so only props you can actually see (plus a margin at the screen edges) cost anything.",""],["0.9.21","Counter-Strike maps, framerate: props in rooms you cannot see into (checked against the map visibility data) and props too small to see at a distance are no longer drawn. Nothing is removed from the map.",""],["0.9.20","Counter-Strike maps: no limit on how many props are built (it used to stop at 5000 props / 170000 triangles). The solid black \"tools/toolsblack\" surfaces that fill some openings are drawn now instead of left empty.",""],["0.9.19","Counter-Strike maps: doors, gates, windows, shutters and wall pieces are built before small clutter, so they are no longer cut off by the prop limit (that left doorways open). Terrain and plaster pieces inside the map are no longer trimmed away either.",""],["0.9.18","Counter-Strike maps: walls and floors that were see-through when viewed from one side are now drawn from both sides (no more holes), scenery near the edge of the map is kept instead of cut off, and the earlier foliage/prop removal stays undone.",""],["0.9.17","Imported maps: Counter-Strike walls and floors are no longer dropped when the middle of a large face falls outside the kept area (that caused see-through holes). Trees, wire and other props are drawn again instead of being left out.",""],["0.9.16","Imported maps: props whose texture cannot be read, or that have cut-out parts (trees, leaves, wire), are left out instead of being drawn as scrambled grey cards.",""],["0.9.15","Imported maps with many props: the props are now chosen biggest first (the old limit kept whichever came first in the file, which on Counter-Strike maps was mostly small clutter), up to 5000 per map, and the import message says how many props were placed.",""],["0.9.14","Prop models from the game files now load. The reader for the model mesh files (.vtx) looked for its tables four bytes too early, so no model could ever be read; it also now copes with the larger strip headers that Counter-Strike: Global Offensive models use and with models that have no bounding box. When a model still cannot be read, the import message says why.",""],["0.9.13","The lobby's map import message now also says whether the Counter-Strike game files were found, how many prop models were loaded, and whether the Wingman layout is on.",""],["0.9.12","Counter-Strike game files: the search for Counter-Strike: Global Offensive now looks inside every Steam library folder it can find (a few levels down, so a different folder layout still works), tries again when you open Settings or import a map instead of giving up after the first miss, and says in Settings and after an import whether it found the files and how many prop models it loaded. If it still cannot find them, linking the \"csgo\" folder with the texture folder button works too.",""],["0.9.11","Counter-Strike maps: the game now finds Counter-Strike: Global Offensive (\"csgo legacy\" or \"Counter-Strike Global Offensive\" in any of your Steam libraries) by itself and uses its files for the props, models and textures of CS:GO maps. Model files inside the game's archives could not be read at all before; they can now, for every Source game. Terrain and ground far outside the map are no longer loaded or walkable: CS:GO maps are limited to the area around their lights, sounds, spawns and props.",""],["0.9.10","Counter-Strike maps import much better. The playable area is now found from the map's own geometry instead of a box around the spawn points, so the ends of maps like Inferno are no longer cut off, and the faraway 3D skybox is left out. Breakable and see-through map pieces and the props placed as entities (crates, barrels, carts) are now included. Maps that carry a small 2 vs 2 layout (Inferno does) can be imported as Wingman: tick \"Small (Wingman) layout\" on the Custom map screen or in the lobby, and the blocker walls, the 2v2 spawn points and the one reachable bomb site are used. Spawn points that the map keeps switched off are no longer used in the normal layout.",""],["0.9.9","High textures: far less grime, cracks and dirt (clean surfaces stay clean, dirt now collects in the grooves), and the 3D props are now textured too. Crates, barrels, tables, shelves, chests, pillars, cars and the rest get real wood grain, brushed metal, stone, painted and foliage surfaces over their normal colours, and round objects are smoother. Works in both the hardware and software renderers.",""],["0.9.8","New anti-aliasing option (Settings > Rendering): Off, 2x, 4x or 8x MSAA to smooth jagged edges. It only shows when Hardware (GPU) rendering is working. Also shortened a lot of the longer text in the settings menu.",""],["0.9.7","The shop ceiling and walls are slightly taller, so the top of the scratch-offs sign no longer pokes through the roof.",""],["0.9.6","New High texture quality: 256x256 textures made to look like real materials instead of drawings, with per-brick and per-tile variation, grime, cracks, chipped edges, surface relief and muted natural colours, on walls, floors, ceilings, shops, arcades, stations and every floor type. The texture options are now called Low (was Classic), Medium (was Enhanced) and High. High costs more memory and a longer load at the start of a floor, so it is meant for faster computers.",""],["0.9.5","Multiplayer: the Barrier Projector now has 150 health and loses health from the damage of each shot that hits it, instead of breaking after a number of hits. Battle royale chests no longer hold powers that do nothing there (Climbing Hooks, Thinned Herd, Second Opinion, Heart Overflow and Corpse Bomb).",""],["0.9.4","Three new capes in Loot Boxes: Frostmantle, Toxic Cloak and Sunforged Mantle.",""],["0.9.3","Vhaloru has 5% more health.",""],["0.9.2","Powers in the Tab menu now show (Max) in red when you have the most of them you can.",""],["0.9.1","Chain Lightning is now capped at 4x. The game version number is now 0.9.1.",""],["0.103","Wel Worn Helm is back to its original look. It can no longer be found in Loot Boxes and only shows in the cosmetics menu once you own it.",""],["0.102","Wel Worn Helm rebuilt to follow your sketch: a beveled crest block with a hole running down over a red almond brow plate, a thin blade behind it, big swept side flares, slanted green eyes, an open grille mouth and a chin block, with many more polygons than before.",""],["0.101","New hat: Wel Worn Helm (Rare, from loot boxes). A battered dark navy helm with a notched crest, a red brow plate, glowing green eye slits, a silver jaw guard and swept side guards.",""],["0.100","The locked Alien Mask in the collection now shows \"???\" instead of the Ashen Knight hint (\"Beat the floor 10 Knight\"), like the other secrets.",""],["0.99","Vhaloru: the time you have to look away from the Unblinking's gaze attack is cut in half (2.7 s to 1.35 s in phase 1, 2.1 s to 1.05 s in phase 2), and the charging whine is shortened to match.",""],["0.98","Past floor 50, enemy health and damage grow 6% per floor instead of 5%.",""],["0.97","Ghost windows: the Arena arcade check used to scan your Steam folders on the same thread that keeps the game window responsive, right at start-up, which can make Windows treat the window as \"Not Responding\" and leave ghost windows in Alt-Tab. That work now runs on its own thread and starts 8 seconds after launch. Closing the game also hides the window instantly and force-ends the process after 2.5 seconds if it has not exited.",""],["0.96","Enemy counts keep growing after floor 32: floor 33 has 33 enemies, floor 34 has 34, and so on up to 50 (boss floors are unchanged).",""],["0.95","Executioner is now capped at 3 copies (it was 4) and Corpse Bomb at 4 copies.",""],["0.94","Patch notes: the in-game patch notes list now shows every version again (0.84 to 0.93 had been merged into the 0.83 entry by a formatting slip).",""],["0.93","Alien levels: chests have their own look. A pearl reliquary with a glowing hex body, sigil panel and a floating gem, and a cursed version that is dark with a slit-pupil eye, crystal thorns and magenta glow. Both are also in the model viewer.",""],["0.92","Stat powers that rolled a good value (like Plated Vest) are now labelled Uncommon instead of Rare, since real Rare powers are a separate thing.",""],["0.91","Weapons: hidden inner faces of gun models (like the Lance top strip, which popped over the body while reloading) are now removed, so they can no longer show through while moving or reloading.",""],["0.90","Weapons: parts of gun models that shared the same flat surface (Lance, Pistol, Scattergun, Twin Fang, Needler, Marksman, melee weapons and more) caused flickering lines and bits appearing or vanishing while moving or reloading. Overlapping surfaces are now pushed apart by a tiny amount so the models look the same.",""],["0.89","Tab menu with many powers: the Weapon and Run box is now full width (side by side), so there is no empty space beside it.",""],["0.88","Plated Vest is capped at 6 copies. Heart Overflow description shortened. The Tab menu with lots of powers now lays them out in columns across the full width (with a visible thin scrollbar), so long lists are no longer cut off.",""],["0.87","Shops: the power items on the shelves (Second Opinion, Plated Vest and others) no longer flicker with lines while you move; overlapping flat faces are pushed apart by a tiny amount, so the designs look the same.",""],["0.86","Shops: the SALE sticker on special deals now shows all four letters (the L was missing).",""],["0.85","City floors: the shop, library and arcade doors can no longer be wiped out by alleys or by rubble on ruined cities, so every city floor has an enterable shop (and library). Shops on alien cities now have the green sign on the door like the arcade and library.",""],["0.84","Floor 25: the Skyfall Warden boss is no longer upside down (talons hang below, head on top).",""],["0.83","Floor 25: the level label in the top left says Castle (it said the underlying cave theme), and gravity in the castle is now normal instead of a quarter of normal, so jumps are no longer floaty.",""],["0.82","Singleplayer: when an enemy kills you, the results screen shows its name, health, damage, speed and traits, plus a small map with you and the killer marked (flashing red ring). Settings > Controls has a new Crosshair editor: line length, gap, thickness, center dot, circle, opacity, color, outline and T shape, with live previews, saved automatically.",""],["0.81","New title: Withered (a Rare loot box title).",""],["0.80","Power names use proper capitalization everywhere (Phase Step, Gravity Well, Frag Grenade, Quick Hands and so on).",""],["0.79","Hearts are no longer wasted: at full health you walk over them and they stay. New regular power Heart overflow: a heart eaten at full health gives +2 Overhealth (max 20; with Overheal too, the max is 40). Messiah now lasts 8 seconds instead of 5.",""],["0.78","Multiplayer: a player's equipped title now shows on their profile card in the lobby (it was only sent during matches before). The game music is 25% quieter; the Music slider keeps its range, so its 100% is the new, quieter level.",""],["0.77","Air Hockey multiplayer: the host can now move to the Spectators and watch. The first player then runs the table for the match.",""],["0.76","Game mode names now use proper capitalization everywhere (Battle Royale, Capture the Flag, Team Deathmatch, Bomb Defusal, Air Hockey and so on).",""],["0.75","Arms Race: a kill no longer swaps your gun mid-round; the new gun arrives with the next round (a feed line tells you which). Battle royale and One in the Chamber: after you are eliminated the kill replay now ends and you can spectate the remaining players (Q / E or the mouse buttons to switch); before, the replay looped forever.",""],["0.74","Floor 25: fixed the lab doorway staying blocked after beating the Warden. A glowing trim strip ran straight across the open door at head height and was solid; it now stops at the doorway.",""],["0.73","Desktop: closing the game now makes sure every game process ends (cleans up Steam, Discord and the lobby server, then force-exits after 1.5 seconds), to stop leftover ghost windows in Alt-Tab.",""],["0.72","Profiles: a player's equipped title now shows in front of their name on their profile card (lobby click and your own preview).",""],["0.71","Title screen: click the version number in the bottom left to open the patch notes (from the readme). It shows what changed since the version you were on before your last update, with a button to show every version.",""],["0.70","Arena machine: removed the long help text from the fullscreen top bar so the bar is slim.",""],["0.69","Arcade: the other machines have plain black screens. Playing Arena now shows a first-person view of you at the machine with the game running on its monitor; Alt+Enter (or the Fullscreen button) switches to the full-window view and back.",""],["0.68","Arena machine: fixed the game's own mount lines (drive written as \"C:\") not being resolved, which left Arena unable to start.",""],["0.67","Arcade Arena machine now uses the game's own DOSBox config (.conf files in its Steam folder: settings and launch commands) instead of guessed settings, keeps the game folder layout, and has a Log button to show what DOSBox is doing.",""],["0.66","Arcade: if The Elder Scrolls: Arena is installed in your Steam library, one arcade machine is switched on and runs it (DOSBox inside the game window; desktop app only; saved games are kept between visits; F12 leaves the machine).",""],["0.65","Shop no-jumping sign is shorter and sits closer to the exit sign.",""],["0.64","The shop no-jumping sign now says \"NO JUMPING\" so it is obvious what it means.",""],["0.63","Added a silly \"no jumping\" sign on the shop wall next to the exit.",""],["0.62","You can no longer jump inside shops (your head went through the ceiling).",""],["0.61","Custom Music now replaces the game's own music on levels that have it (Shops, Space station, Castle, Coliseum) so the two never play over each other. Those levels are marked with an asterisk in Settings > Audio > Custom Music.",""],["0.60","Settings > Audio now has a \"Custom Music\" submenu. The general YouTube link moved into it, and each level theme (Dungeon, Cavern, Lab, Crypt, Manor, Foundry, City, Mineshaft, Coliseum, Bandit hideout, Space station, Castle, Shops) can have its own YouTube link that plays instead of the general one on those levels.",""],["0.59","Debug mode: new \"Cutscene viewer\" button on the main menu under Sound tester. It plays the alien home world, the space elevator, the station crash (escape and left-behind), the ending and the coliseum boss entrance on their own, and returns to the list when each one ends.",""],["0.58","Cat Ears: the black part is larger so they read clearly as cat ears.",""],["0.57","New hat: Cat Ears (Uncommon), black ears with pink insides on a thin headband. Drops from loot boxes.",""],["0.56","New hat: Oni Horns (Rare), two stubby yellow ridged horns. It drops from loot boxes like the other hats.",""],["0.55","Reaper axe: the shaft now goes into the iron collar and comes out the other end cleanly (it no longer overlaps the collar faces).",""],["0.54","Reaper axe: replaced the wide box at the top of the shaft (it stuck out of both sides with the shaft clipping through it) with a round mount ring.",""],["0.53","Reaper axe: the hand pegs no longer pass through the shaft (they are short stubs on each side), which fixes the overlapping/clipping look.",""],["0.52","Chest model: a bit more detail. Domed lid, plank grooves, iron plinth, corner brackets, back hinges, rivets on the gold straps, and a lock plate with a keyhole and hasp; cursed chests also get small iron spikes on the lid.",""],["0.51","Linux: BUILD.sh now builds a plain folder (dist/linux-unpacked) that can update itself, and PLAY-LINUX.sh prefers it; the AppImage is still available with ./BUILD.sh appimage. Single-file builds (AppImage, portable .exe) now show an \"update available\" box with a link to the download page instead of staying silent. Rebuild once with the new BUILD.sh to get the self-updating build.",""],["0.50","Reaper axe: removed the dark facet lines from the metal parts too (collar, spike, pommel, hand pegs).",""],["0.49","Reaper axe handle: removed the many dark lines and stripes along the handle; it is now a smooth wooden shaft with two plain grip wraps.",""],["0.48","Fan gun damage +5% in singleplayer (multiplayer unchanged).",""],["0.47","Scattergun damage +5%.",""],["0.46","The game now checks GitHub for a newer version when it starts and offers to install it (Update and restart / Later). It downloads the same checked game-files.zip as Updater.exe and backs up the old files. Turn it off with \"autoUpdate\": false in settings.json. Needs a game folder with resources\\app (not an .asar).",""],["0.45","Added the MIT LICENSE, THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt (credits for the orchestral samples, font, libraries and trademark notes), a GitHub README.md and .gitignore. Updates now come from GitHub: the new Updater.exe downloads the newest game files from the latest release of github.com/EffDeeArr/ad (checked by checksum, old files backed up) and works from any earlier version. Patch-to-*.exe files are no longer made.",""],["0.44","Fixed very low FPS with a frame cap above 60: vsync and the frame limiter are now only switched off when the cap is above the monitor refresh rate (before, any cap over 60 did it). The setting is re-checked at every start, so existing installs correct themselves after one extra restart.",""],["0.43","Startup in borderless fullscreen now waits for the window and game to finish loading before entering fullscreen (was done mid-load; reported to leave some PCs at very low FPS until the setting was toggled).",""],["0.42","Super turret is now only 10% larger than the regular turret. Shots from both player turrets (and enemy turrets) now leave from the barrel tips. Shop power prices are now $40-80, and 2% of powers on the shelves are a SPECIAL DEAL at $30 with a SALE sticker.",""],["0.41","Super turret has its own look: gold armour plating, twin barrels with glowing muzzles, side ammo drums, a radar fin, a glowing base ring and a spinning ring of violet energy around the head, on top of being bigger than the regular turret.",""],["0.40","Two new powers. Afterimage (rare): after you take a hit you cannot be hurt again for 1 second (instead of the usual brief 0.2s). Thinned herd (regular, stacks up to 5): one less regular enemy on every floor per copy.",""],["0.39","Air hockey vs. the Monster now pays $50 for a win instead of $20.",""],["0.38","Shops (and libraries/arcades) now have a textured ceiling: speckled acoustic tiles in a grid with fluorescent light panels. It follows the ruined and alien looks on later floors. Works in both renderers.",""],["0.37","Enhanced mode: the shop shelves (and library bookshelves), the side of the counter and the cabinet now have much more detail: planked backs and sides with wood grain, grained shelf boards, metal brackets and nails, raised door panels with handles, a speckled top on the side counter, and a framed, grained cabinet.",""],["0.36","Alien shops: the wooden shelves, counter, side counter, cabinet and scratch-off stand are now pearl and violet with glowing trim and crystal tips.",""],["0.35","Alien floors: shops and libraries on floors 26+ are now alien (pearl-and-violet room, all signs and posters in alien script, an alien shopkeeper with a halo instead of a human cashier). Before this they showed the ruined look with leftover alien crystals, and the city spires showed through the shop ceiling.",""],["0.34","Alien city: roofs now sit flush on the buildings (the base slab matches the building footprint instead of overhanging and looking like it floats).",""],["0.33","Alien city: every building now has a real 3D spire on top (stacked pearl tiers, a glowing ring floating around it and a glowing crystal tip), replacing the flat pointed shapes. Works in both renderers.",""],["0.32","Alien city: each building now has one large pointed roof over its whole frontage (taller for wider buildings) instead of a row of small spikes.",""],["0.31","Alien floors: the screen effect (light motes and violet vignette) is now much fainter. The alien city now matches the cutscene cities: pearl buildings with pointed roofs, no windows, and every building carries a sign in made-up alien script instead of English, so the only way to tell you can enter one is the green sign on its door.",""],["0.30","After the floor 25 boss falls and the science lab opens, a prototype alien teleporter stands inside: step into the ring and a short 3D cutscene shows the alien home world (floating pearl cities, light bridges, a ringed planet). Space skips it. Floors 26 and up are alien versions of every level theme: pearl-and-crystal walls with glowing veins, a floating-spire skyline, alien props (seed pods, crystal spires, stasis capsules, hover-pods in cities), drifting light motes, and no humans. Not tested on a real GPU or with audio.",""],["0.29","The game keeps its 0.x version style (0.29, 0.30, ...). package.json now stores it in the three-part form the build tools require (0.29.0, 0.30.0, ...); the title screen, patches and updater show it as 0.29. Gameplay is unchanged from 0.28.",""],["0.28","Cold snap model: rebuilt from pieces that only touch instead of three bars passing through each other, which removes the flickering/overlapping faces. Same shape and colors.",""],["0.27","Dungeon shop now only appears on floors with the Dungeon theme (not Lab, Foundry, Manor, Crypt, Cavern, City, Mineshaft, etc.).",""],["0.26","Dungeon shop: about half of ordinary dungeon floors now have a small shop room built into the level: a table with 3 random powers for $50 each (press F next to it), a skull-masked shopkeeper behind it, and two little fires. Buying something makes the shopkeeper say \"It's dangerous to go alone! Take this\". Not on city, mineshaft, boss, special or multiplayer floors.",""],["0.25","Twin daggers deal 25% more damage in singleplayer.",""],["0.24","Floor 25: siege wave monsters now have 50% less health and damage than normal floor 25 monsters (was 25%).",""],["0.23","Floor 25: closed the gap between the lab door steps and the lab floor (grass was visible through it).",""],["0.22","Floor 25: the landing pad beside the lab is now a solid, thicker platform sunk into the ground (it looked like it was floating and its dark sides vanished at some angles).",""],["0.21","Floor 25: the castle gate facing the lab is now open and the other gate is shut (the keep moved to the north end); the lab entrance has steps up to it and is sealed by a force field until the waves and the Skyfall Warden are defeated.",""],["0.20","Floor 25: fixed the flickering stripes on the castle wall beside the gates (two overlapping wall faces were fighting each other).",""],["0.19","Floor 25 is now The Siege: a small stone castle with stairs up to the ramparts. Survive 5 waves of weak monsters (25% less health and damage, no modifiers), walk to the alien science lab, and the Skyfall Warden (a huge mecha bird that drops bombs, fires bolt fans and dives every ~6 seconds) attacks. New real-instrument orchestral battle theme. Textures on this map are 256x256 (the engine now supports 256px textures in both renderers).",""],["0.18","Stuck rescue hardened: it now also fixes a broken (non-numeric) player position, skips remembered safe spots that have since become blocked, and searches fresh if a rescue does not hold.",""],["0.17","Stuck rescue for every mode and floor: if you are inside something for over a second, or hold a movement key for 2.5 seconds while boxed in on every side, you are teleported back to the last safe spot (or the nearest open one).",""],["0.16","Floor 15: respawning after a fall now searches for a valid free spot near the checkpoint (not inside a wall or on a jump pad) and widens the search if you get put back repeatedly, so you can no longer end up unable to move.",""],["0.15","Air hockey: the field is split into four invisible quadrants; a puck that stays in one for 6 straight seconds resets to the middle. Puck hit sounds are rate-limited so they no longer stack into a loud noise.",""],["0.14","Air hockey: if the puck gets pinned in a corner/wall on the monster's side, it is now kicked back toward the middle instead of being pushed there forever.",""],["0.13","DEFLECT text raised; the ready icon is grey during the cooldown and fills with blue from the bottom as it recovers.",""],["0.12","Deflect cues: your melee weapon glows blue and DEFLECT shows at the bottom middle while it is active; a small blue icon of your melee weapon shows there when it is ready again.",""],["0.11","Blink dash now carries you over pits when you have climbing hooks. Melee blocking now cuts damage taken by 50% (was 33%).",""],["0.6","Ashen Knight fires 50% more projectiles in his second phase. New melee-only power \"Deflect\": while blocking, enemy shots are reflected at enemies for the shot's damage (3 s per block, then 6 s cooldown, cannot stack, never offered to gun builds).",""]];
